    {"role": "assistant", "text": "Here's a CTO-ready one-page summary:\n\n---\n\n## Production ML Recommendation System — Architecture Summary\n\n**Scale**: 50M users, 5M items, 500K requests/second peak, p99 < 50ms\n\n### Core Architecture: Two-Tower + ANN\nUser and item representations are computed as 128-dimensional embeddings. At query time, only the user embedding is computed (5-10ms via GPU-served transformer tower). Item embeddings are pre-computed and indexed in FAISS (IVF8192,PQ32), enabling sub-5ms approximate nearest-neighbor search across all 5M items.\n\n### Serving Stack\n- **Kubernetes (EKS)**: GPU inference nodes (g4dn.xlarge, 70% spot) for user tower; memory-optimized nodes (r5.2xlarge) for FAISS; auto-scales 10→200 pods in 3 minutes\n- **Caching**: Tiered Redis strategy — 2M hot user embeddings (1GB), 10M warm compressed embeddings (1.3GB), cold users computed on-demand\n- **Zero-downtime deploys**: Rolling K8s updates with readiness probes; blue-green FAISS index swap\n\n### Training Pipeline (Daily)\nEvent collection (500M events/day) → Kafka → Feature computation (Spark, 45min) → Two-tower training with in-batch negatives (GPU cluster, 2h) → Evaluation gate (Hit Rate@10, NDCG@10) → Auto-deploy if metrics improve → Item index rebuild\n\n### Model Architecture\n- **User tower**: Hybrid transformer (50-item sequence) + MLP (static features), GPU-served\n- **Item tower**: Content features (text, category, image) + behavioral stats, with masked cold-start handling\n- **Objective**: Multi-objective — CTR primary, with constraints on revenue contribution, catalog coverage, and freshness\n\n### Real-Time Personalization\nFlink streaming processes user events sub-second → session features (last 20 items, current category) stored in Redis → combined with 15-min batch user embeddings at query time\n\n### Key Metrics\n- Latency: user tower ~8ms GPU, FAISS ~3ms, total ~15ms (well within 50ms SLA)\n- Cache hit rate: >88% (absorbs most traffic before model inference)\n- Index freshness: 30-min delta updates, weekly full rebuild\n- Model freshness: daily retraining, auto-promoted if Hit Rate@10 improves ≥0.5%\n\n### Cost Profile (Monthly)\n- Infrastructure: ~$14K (EKS, Redis, Kafka, S3)\n- Per-user cost: ~$0.28/month at full scale\n- Key savings: spot instances (60% GPU discount), model quantization (2x throughput), tiered caching (90% Redis cost reduction)\n\n### Outstanding Decisions\n1. FAISS IVF vs HNSW: run accuracy benchmark (2 days)\n2. Transformer layer ablation for user tower latency/accuracy tradeoff (1 week)\n3. RL for sequential recommendations: assess in Q3 after current architecture stabilizes\n\n---\n\nThis architecture is production-ready and based on patterns from recommendation systems at similar scale (DoorDash, Pinterest, LinkedIn). Expected timeline: 3 months to MVP, 6 months to full production.", "index": 47},
