    {"role": "assistant", "text": "Disaster recovery for an ML serving system has unique challenges compared to CRUD applications — you have stateful components (FAISS index, Redis cache, trained models) that are expensive to replicate.\n\n**RTO/RPO Targets:**\nFirst, establish targets with stakeholders:\n- **RTO (Recovery Time Objective)**: How long can the service be down? For recommendations: 5-15 minutes acceptable (site still works, just defaults to popular items)\n- **RPO (Recovery Point Objective)**: How much data loss is acceptable? Model staleness of 24h is fine. FAISS index staleness of 1h is acceptable.\n\n**Multi-Region Architecture:**\n\n```\nRegion: us-east-1 (primary)\n  Full stack: inference, training, FAISS, Redis, Kafka\n  \nRegion: eu-west-1 (secondary — warm standby)\n  Reduced stack: inference only, Redis replica, FAISS read replica\n  Updated every 30min from primary\n  Can serve recommendations at 70% capacity immediately\n  \nRegion: ap-southeast-1 (tertiary — cold standby)\n  S3 model/index backups only\n  Spin up in 15-30 minutes\n```\n\n**Replication strategy for stateful components:**\n\n```python\n# FAISS index replication\n# Every 30 min, after index rebuild completes:\n# 1. Upload new index to S3 in all regions\naws s3 cp faiss_index.bin s3://ml-models-eu/indices/ --region eu-west-1\naws s3 cp faiss_index.bin s3://ml-models-ap/indices/ --region ap-southeast-1\n\n# 2. Secondary regions pull and hot-swap (same blue-green pattern)\n# Secondary FAISS updater runs on 30-min schedule\n\n# Redis: Cross-region replication via ElastiCache Global Datastore\n# Primary in us-east-1, read replica in eu-west-1\n# Replication lag: typically <100ms\n```\n\n**Graceful degradation — the fallback stack:**\n```python\nasync def get_recommendations_with_fallback(user_id):\n    try:\n        # Primary: personalized FAISS + user embedding\n        return await get_personalized_recommendations(user_id)\n    except ServiceUnavailable:\n        try:\n            # Fallback 1: cached recommendations (might be stale by 1h)\n            cached = await redis.get(f'cached_recs:{user_id}')\n            if cached:\n                return deserialize(cached)\n        except RedisUnavailable:\n            pass\n        \n        # Fallback 2: editorial/trending recommendations (no ML)\n        return get_trending_items(category=user.last_known_category, k=10)\n```\n\n**Trending items as ultimate fallback:**\nMaintain a pre-computed 'trending items per category' list, updated hourly and stored in S3. This requires no ML infrastructure and can be served from a CDN. If everything else fails, serve this. Users get non-personalized but at least relevant recommendations.\n\n**Chaos Engineering:**\nRunning GameDays is the only reliable way to validate DR:\n```bash\n# Monthly chaos test\n# Randomly kill 50% of inference pods\nkubectl delete pods -l app=inference-server \\\n  --field-selector status.phase=Running \\\n  -n production \\\n  $(kubectl get pods ... | shuf | head -n 25)\n\n# Verify p99 latency stays < 100ms\n# Verify no 5xx errors to users\n```\n\n**RTO achievement:**\n- Primary region failure → eu-west-1 takes over: ~2-3 min (DNS failover + health check propagation)\n- eu-west-1 capacity: 70% of primary (pre-warmed)\n- Full recovery with us-east-1 restored: ~10-15 min", "index": 49},
