    {"role": "assistant", "text": "Data privacy for recommendation systems is increasingly regulated and often underestimated in architectural planning. Here's what you need to address for GDPR (EU) and CCPA (California) compliance:\n\n**Key Legal Requirements:**\n\n**Right to Erasure ('Right to be Forgotten'):**\nWhen a user requests deletion, you must remove:\n1. Raw event data (Kafka, S3 event store)\n2. Derived features (Redis feature cache)\n3. User embedding (Redis + cold storage)\n4. Training data inclusion (retroactive model retraining or proof model doesn't memorize individuals)\n\n```python\nasync def handle_erasure_request(user_id):\n    # Step 1: Immediate — remove from serving path\n    await redis.delete(f'ue:{user_id}')           # User embedding\n    await redis.delete(f'rt_features:{user_id}')  # Real-time features\n    await redis.delete(f'cached_recs:{user_id}')  # Cached recs\n    \n    # Step 2: Async — remove from data lake\n    kafka_producer.send('erasure_requests', {'user_id': user_id})\n    # Downstream Spark job will purge from S3 event store (within 30 days, per GDPR)\n    \n    # Step 3: Model handling\n    # Log erasure in audit trail\n    db.insert('erasure_audit', {'user_id': user_id, 'timestamp': now(), 'status': 'pending'})\n    # On next weekly model retrain, the user's data is excluded\n    # Model is considered compliant after next retrain\n```\n\n**Data Minimization:**\nOnly collect what's strictly necessary for recommendations:\n```python\n# BAD: Store full page URL (contains PII in URL params)\nevent = {'user_id': uid, 'url': 'shop.com/user/12345/orders', 'item_id': iid}\n\n# GOOD: Store only what's needed for recommendations\nevent = {'user_id': uid, 'item_id': iid, 'event_type': 'view', 'timestamp': ts}\n```\n\n**Pseudonymization:**\nNever store user emails or names in the recommendation pipeline. Use only pseudonymous user IDs:\n```python\n# User ID mapping service (separate, locked-down service)\ndef get_rec_user_id(email):\n    return hmac_sha256(email, secret_key=REC_SYSTEM_SECRET)[:16]\n# email → deterministic pseudonym; reversible only with secret key\n```\n\n**Consent Management:**\nFor GDPR, personalized recommendations require explicit consent in the EU:\n```python\ndef get_recommendations(user_id, consent):\n    if consent.personalization_allowed:\n        return personalized_recommendations(user_id)\n    else:\n        # Non-personalized: popular items in user's browsed categories only\n        # No user-specific model, no embedding storage\n        return editorial_recommendations(user.country)\n```\n\n**Data Residency:**\nFor EU users, interaction data may need to stay in EU data centers:\n```python\n# Route EU users to EU inference stack\nif user.country in EU_COUNTRIES:\n    endpoint = 'https://api-eu.recommendations.com'\nelse:\n    endpoint = 'https://api-us.recommendations.com'\n```\n\nThis has significant infrastructure implications — you may need completely separate model training pipelines per region.\n\n**Audit Trail:**\nMaintain immutable logs of what recommendations were served to each user:\n```python\n# Immutable recommendation audit log\naudit_log.append({\n    'user_id': user_id,\n    'session_id': session_id,\n    'timestamp': now(),\n    'model_version': MODEL_VERSION,\n    'recommendations': [item_ids],\n    'context_features_hash': sha256(str(features)),  # Hash not raw features\n})\n```\nThis audit trail is essential for GDPR Article 22 compliance (right to explanation of automated decisions).", "index": 51},
